UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventthegreatestdiscoveryinmodernmedicineandavirusthatisnomore26153-20260924@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20260924T145220Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:The Greatest Discovery in Modern Medicine (and a Virus That Is No More)
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Edward Jenner first tested the world's first successful smallpox vaccine in 1796\, making a significant advance over the ancient practice of variolation against this ancient and devastating infectious disease. One hundred and eighty-four years later\, smallpox was declared eradicated from the planet by the World Health Organization\, the only microorganism to no longer circulate in the human population due to deliberate human intervention. The Microbiology\, Public Health & History film festival at Hood College celebrates International Microorganism Day 2026 by observing the 230th anniversary of Dr. Jenner's critical discovery. We will begin our fifth season with a screening of the 2010 BBC documentary\, \\
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-greatest-discovery-in-modern-medicine-(and-a-virus-that-is-no-more)/26153/
END:VEVENT
